winch secret: manage secrets and the age key

Examples:
  # make your age key and add it to the recipients
  winch secret init
  # write a random password into the inventory
  winch secret generate vars.monit_password
  # encrypt the content of a file
  winch secret encrypt < dkim.key
  # encrypt the output of a command
  openssl rand -hex 16 | winch secret encrypt
  # encrypt all secrets again after a change of the recipients
  winch secret rekey

Usage:
  winch secret <command>

Secret encrypts values with age for the recipients in winch.yaml.

winch reads the age key from the stdout of the command in
WINCH_AGE_IDENTITY_CMD, which runs through sh -c. Without it, winch
reads the file that WINCH_AGE_KEY names, or else
~/.config/winch/age.key. Both variables set is an error.

Commands:
  init      add an age key to the recipients
  generate  write a random password as a secret
  encrypt   encrypt a value from stdin
  rekey     encrypt all secrets again

Run "winch secret <command> --help" for the arguments and flags of a
command.

See: winch doc secrets
